1. Problem Statement
Calculate current attendance percentage from attended and total classes held, determine eligibility against a minimum threshold (75%), and calculate the minimum consecutive upcoming classes a student must attend to recover eligibility under various future scenarios.

2. Objectives
•	Compute current attendance percentage accurately.
•	Determine exact recovery deficit in terms of consecutive future classes.
•	Simulate future scenarios based on anticipated upcoming schedule.

3. Assumptions
•	Attended classes cannot exceed total classes conducted.
•	Student will attend 100% of upcoming recovery classes.

4. Algorithm
1. Read attended classes (A) and total held classes (T).
2. Current Percentage = (A / T) * 100.
3. If Percentage >= 75%, student is eligible (0 recovery classes needed).
4. Else, calculate required future classes N such that (A + N) / (T + N) >= 0.75.
5. N = ceil((0.75 * T - A) / (1 - 0.75)) = ceil((3*T - 4*A)).
6. Display current status and required recovery classes.

